he workflow change itself.\n\nOne alternative is testing in a scratch repo pointing pi-action at this branch's SHA directly, avoiding any main change entirely — though the user probably wants the real thing tested here, so I should mention that as a secondary option.\n\nI want to check whether pi-action's extensions input actually supports a `github:cv/pit#<sha>` style reference, so let me look at the pi-action README quickly.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"[Pit: collapsed typescript call · \"Check how pi-action v2.5.4 resolves the extensions input\" · gh.api · ok · ~1.0K tokens · originals: session.inspectEntry(\"23\"), session.inspectEntry(\"25\")]"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":1804,"cacheRead":44723,"cacheWrite":2423,"totalTokens":48952,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":1551},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1794909054022,"responseId":"msg_bdrk_q4n4uvc3vmz7hmgfyvdtyeupkogxtttyomlyxr3i7pnpxk6nibkq","rawStopReason":"tool_use","durationMs":24184,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}]},{"target":25,"action":"omit"},{"target":27,"action":"replace","messages":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Since installs happen without lifecycle scripts, Pit must run straight from source rather than a built dist, which means any commit SHA works the same way a tag does. The comment-run checkout uses main, and for this PR the extension comes from the head SHA against the main workspace, so that's consistent. Time to implement.\n\nI need to figure out how to detect the PR context across event types — issue_comment, pull_request opened, and pull_request_review_comment each expose labels and PR number differently, so I'm planning a bash step to normalize the number and check for a specific label like \"pit-from-pr\" via the GitHub API, then confirm the head repo match